        "content": "=== np_zap ===\nDescription: Zap a wand in the given cardinal (n, e, s, w) or ordinal direction (ne, se, sw, nw) or target yourself using self.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_pickup ===\nDescription: Pickup things at your location or specify where you want to pickup an item.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_up ===\nDescription: Go up a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_down ===\nDescription: Go down a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_loot ===\nDescription: Loot a box on the floor.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_offer ===\nDescription: Offer a sacrifice to the gods.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_drop ===\nDescription: Drop an item.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_read ===\nDescription: Read a scroll, spellbook, or something else.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_put_on ===\nDescription: Put on an accessory.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_remove ===\nDescription: Remove an accessory (ring, amulet, or blindfold).\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_takeoff ===\nDescription: Take off one piece of armor.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_wield ===\nDescription: Wield a weapon.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_wear ===\nDescription: Wear a piece of armor.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_apply ===\nDescription: Apply (use) a tool. If used on a wand, that wand will be broken, releasing its magic in the process.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_eat ===\nDescription: Eat something from your inventory or straight from the ground.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_drink ===\nDescription: Drink something from your inventory or straight from the ground.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_tip ===\nDescription: Tip out the content of a container.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_dip ===\nDescription: Dip an object into something.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_kick ===\nDescription: Kick something.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_rest ===\nDescription: Rests n-moves while doing nothing or until something happens (default=5).\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_cast ===\nDescription: Opens your spellbook to cast a spell.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_pay ===\nDescription: Pay your shopping bill.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_pray ===\nDescription: Pray to the gods for help.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_look ===\nDescription: Look at what is under you.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_set_avoid_monster_flag ===\nDescription: If set to true skills will try to avoid monsters.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_melee_attack ===\nDescription: Pursues and attacks a given target using melee attacks until it is dead.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_explore_level ===\nDescription: Explores the level to find new rooms, as well as hidden doors and corridors.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_move_to ===\nDescription: Move to the specified position using pathfinding.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_go_to ===\nDescription: Moves to the specified room or corridor using the shortest path possible.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_press_key ===\nDescription: Presses the given letter. For special keys only ESC, SPACE, and ENTER are supported.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== np_type_text ===\nDescription: Types the text by pressing the keys in order.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== reveal ===\nDescription: Reveal a rectangular region of the dungeon map as ASCII (for the bounding-box observation mode, where the map is otherwise hidden). Coordinates are map cells: x = column 0-78, y = row 0-20, inclusive. The FULL map (x1=0, y1=0, x2=78, y2=20) is a valid request and returns all 79 columns. Returns the sub-rectangle as text; consumes NO game turn. Out-of-range requests are clamped to the grid, and any clamping is stated in the reply.\nSchema: {}\n\n=== rollback ===\nDescription: Undo the last n turns, returning the game to the state it was in before them. Use after a mistake -- walking into a losing fight, triggering a trap, wasting turns in a dead end. Costs one turn and no game time. n must be between 1 and 15.\nSchema: {}\n\n",
